the silver. Romashkova never really factored for the gold but won the bronze. Fikotová also made headlines during the Olympics because she began a much publicized East-West romance with American hammer thrower, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78255"} "Hal Connolly"] ". Overcoming what was described as “mountains of red tape” they fell in love and were married in Praha three months after the Olympics, with Czech distance running legend " [:a {:href "/athletes/76736"} "Emil Zátopek"] " serving as best man, although Connolly and Fikotová would divorce in 1973. Fikotová-Connolly would eventually compete in five Olympics, the next four representing the United States."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "592"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77826"} "Olga Fikotová"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TCH"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TCH.png"}] "TCH"]] [:td {} "50.77 (1)"] [:td {} "53.69 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "600"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77156"} "Irina Beglyakova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "47.65 (3)"] [:td {} "52.54 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "601"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77292"} "Nina Romashkova-Ponomaryova"]] [:td {} [:a {:h